ng if the weapon gets into the right  hands but it could also be a complete  disaster if it ever gets into the wrong  hands now odin clearly wanted to open  mono to the outside world and yet when  he returned to wano odin did not open  its borders assuming odin knew about  pluton because he did after all go to  laugh tale it seems clear that he could  have used pluton to defeat kaido but he  didn't do it i believe that the reason  why odin didn't activate pluton is  directly related to the reason why roger  believed that he was too early and that  he still had to wait for someone in  order for pluton to be properly used  poseidon had to be reborn and joy boy  had to return so that is why odin  allowed himself to be killed by kaido  and rochi instead of just using pluton  to destroy them both i'll get back to  poseidon joy boy and uranus in a little  bit but first let's talk about what  pluton actually is it seems clear to me  that pluton can only be one thing pluton  is nuana itself after the ancient  kingdom lost the war 800 years ago they  decided to protect pluton by placing it  on top of old wano and then sealing it  off from the outside world using those  gigantic walls pluton is not just any  battleship it is a gigantic island-sized  battleship that has been hiding in plain  sight this entire time this is why  everyone who actually saw the blueprint  was absolutely shocked at the sight of  them as experienced shipbuilders people  like frankie rob lucci and kaku knew  that these blueprints were real but they  couldn't believe that something of that  size and scale had actually been built  and that brings me back to the words  that were used to describe the current  state of pluton on wano pluton was said  to be asleep or resting rather than  being turned off or inactive or  decommissioned  this implies that while pluton is a  highly advanced battleship it may not be  an inanimate object pluton may actually  be an organic battleship a battleship  that was built 